    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a derived `timezone` field to the owner response, sourced from a fixed region-to-timezone table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nThe logic is placed where it belongs, reusing the existing locality pipeline rather than duplicating it:\n\n1. **`model/CityRegion.java`** \u2014 the class that already owns the region reference data (city\u2192region, region\u2192postcode ranges) now also holds the `REGION_TIMEZONES` table and a `timezoneOf(String region)` lookup. Returns `null` for `UNKNOWN`/unmapped regions, consistent with the existing `rangeOf`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 a small `timezone(Owner)` method derives the timezone from the owner's already-computed `locality(owner)` via `CityRegion.timezoneOf(...)`, wired with `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)`. No re-derivation of the region.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` property to the Owner schema (right after `locality`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion`, asserting `$.locality == NSW` and `$.timezone == Australia/Sydney` for a Sydney/2000 owner) and the full suite pass: **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
